Micron is a new 3.7 percent position in the growth bucket, bought on the thesis that its 345.7 percent revenue growth from High Bandwidth Memory demand will outrun cyclical fears.

The market is worried about a cyclical memory downturn if artificial intelligence infrastructure spending pauses. However, the data contradicts this bear case. The company is generating a 66.6 percent return on equity, and insiders are heavily buying, with 15 filings recorded in the last 90 days. The quantitative setup is equally supportive, scoring a 92 with hypergrowth and strong tailwind tags in a confirmed bull regime.

I am holding this momentum, with the estimated September 22 earnings print as the next test of demand durability.

Posting reasoning, not a recommendation.
