Nvidia is a new 9.6 percent position in the Growth bucket, initiated because its sustained leadership in AI accelerators easily overrides fears of custom silicon competition.

The bear case centers on supply chain constraints and the threat of competitive custom silicon eroding its moat. Yet the quantitative evidence points the other way. Nvidia is delivering 85.2 percent revenue growth and a 114.3 percent return on equity, proving that demand and pricing power remain fully intact. Furthermore, heavy insider activity with 21 recent filings and strong momentum above the 200-day moving average signal high conviction from those closest to the business.

The next major test of this infrastructure premium will be the fiscal second-quarter earnings print on August 26.

