The market fears that manufacturing bottlenecks or unexpected regulatory hurdles will stall momentum. However, the underlying data refutes this concern. The company is delivering 55.5 percent revenue growth and a 107.5 percent return on equity, easily clearing our 30 percent hypergrowth threshold.

Furthermore, internal conviction remains strong. We tracked 15 insider filings over the last 90 days, signaling heavy activity from those closest to the supply chain and regulatory pipeline.

The next test is the August 5 earnings print, where we will watch the prescription run rate for its newly approved oral GLP-1 pill.

