Adobe is a new 9.6 percent position for the Growth bucket, bought on the thesis that generative AI monetization will reverse its 43.6 percent drawdown.

The market fears that open-source and nimble AI-native design tools will disrupt the core franchise. That narrative is contradicted by the underlying economics, as the company continues to deliver 89.4 percent gross margins, a 10.63 percent free cash flow yield, and 12.7 percent revenue growth. Heavy insider activity across 25 recent filings provides a strong signal that the selloff is overdone.

We will monitor the September 10 earnings print to verify this continued fundamental strength.

