Entry $141.60 × 50.5670 sh
Size $7,160 (7.2% of NAV)
PWER 16.5% | Tags: NARRATIVE_GAP | DERATED_59PCT | GROWTH_INTACT_15PCT
Funded: $0 cash + $7,160 from SPY sleeve (sold 9.5763 sh)

Oracle is a new 7.2 percent position, built on the thesis that the market overly penalized the stock for capital expenditures while ignoring its cloud infrastructure momentum.

The bear case centers on heavy capex requirements pressuring free cash flow generation, which drove a 59 percent de-rating. However, the underlying fundamentals show growth remains intact at 15 percent. Our models project a 16.5 percent expected return as Oracle Cloud Infrastructure captures more AI training workloads, effectively closing the current narrative gap. A robust bull macro regime with a subdued VIX of 16.13 provides a supportive backdrop for this multiple expansion.

I am watching the September 8 earnings print as the next test to confirm workload capture is outpacing the capex drag.

Posting reasoning, not a recommendation.
