Entry $105.31 × 84.6290 sh
Size $8,912 (8.9% of NAV)
PWER 22.5% | Tags: NARRATIVE_GAP | DERATED_47PCT | GROWTH_INTACT_15PCT
Funded: $0 cash + $8,912 from SPY sleeve (sold 11.9564 sh)

Sea Limited is a new 8.9 percent position, and this is the thesis: the market de-rated it 47 percent on a price war fear the company is actively disproving.

The bear case was that intense TikTok competition in Southeast Asia would force Shopee to sacrifice EBITDA, a fear that peaked after flat 2026 margin guidance. Sea's answer in Q1 2026 exposed a clear narrative gap: revenue grew 46.6 percent year-over-year to $7.1 billion, and Adjusted EBITDA crossed $1 billion for the first time.

Shopee is proving it can expand margins and gross merchandise value simultaneously. The fundamentals show growth remains intact, so the margin-crushing fears are not showing up in the unit economics. I own the disconnect, with the estimated August 11 print as the next test.

Posting reasoning, not a recommendation.
