2026-07-09 21:47:49,649 | INFO | 🟢 BUY AXON [GROWTH]
Entry $582.00 × 7.0763 sh
Size $4,118 (4.1% of NAV)
PWER 26.5% | Tags: NARRATIVE_GAP | DERATED_34PCT | GROWTH_INTACT_15PCT
Funded: $0 cash + $4,118 from SPY sleeve (sold 5.4787 sh)

Axon is a new 4.1 percent Growth position where a software and cloud mix shift is driving gross margin expansion and multiple re-rating. 

The market de-rated the stock 34 percent on fears that municipal budget constraints will delay large-scale hardware deployments and contract renewals. Yet this narrative gap ignores the actual unit economics. The company is delivering 33.7 percent year-over-year revenue growth and 59.5 percent gross margins because its transition to a hardware-plus-software model is already working. With baseline growth intact at 15 percent and a confirmed macro bull market providing a constructive backdrop for equity risk, the fundamental evidence directly contradicts the municipal spending bear case. 

I am buying the disconnect, with the August 3 earnings print serving as the next test of this software transition.

Posting reasoning, not a recommendation.
